WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.630
- [Reporter] Kobe Bryant,
one of the greatest players

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:05.970
in NBA history died in a
helicopter crash on Sunday

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.040
at the age of 41.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.400
His 13-year-old daughter

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.930
and several others onboard also died.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:14.340
Bryant, known by his
nickname, Black Mamba,

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.410
is being mourned as being one
of the best basketball players

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.660
of his generation.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.250
- [Jason] Kobe Bryant straddles a couple

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.910
of different eras of basketball.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:26.250
He goes from the sort
of smash-up, mash-up era

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.550
of the '90s where you had
tough teams like the Miami Heat

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.200
and the Knicks to the kind

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.730
of perimeter-focused three-point shooting

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.018
that you see nowadays.

00:00:35.018 --> 00:00:37.320
- [Reporter] In two
decades with the Lakers,

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.876
the 18-time all-star
won five championships

00:00:39.876 --> 00:00:44.420
and scored 33,643 points.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.450
The fourth most in NBA history.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:47.360
- [Jason] He could do it all.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.350
I mean, that was one of his great gifts

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:50.793
as a basketball player.

00:00:50.793 --> 00:00:52.166
He wasn't wedded to any one style.

00:00:52.166 --> 00:00:54.000
He could beat you inside, outside.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.100
He could beat you seemingly
single handedly in his prime.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.270
- [Reporter] In 1996, after
graduating from high school

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:03.170
outside Philadelphia, he
elected to skip college

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:05.030
and go straight to the NBA

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:08.340
where he was drafted 13th
overall by the Charlotte Hornets

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.587
and immediately traded
to the Los Angeles Lakers

00:01:10.587 --> 00:01:12.770
where he quickly became a star.

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:14.830
- The crowd got me real
pumped up after the dunk.

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.330
- [Reporter] As a rookie, we
won the slam dunk contests

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:20.940
and in his second year was
chosen to be an all-star.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.570
His meteoric rise continued
through the late '90s

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:25.340
and into the early 2000s.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:27.350
Bryant, alongside
teammate Shaquille O'Neal

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.750
and coach Phil Jackson by 2002

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.260
had won three consecutive
NBA championships.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:34.680
- [Reporter] A three peak NS sweep.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.480
- [Reporter] The next year,
Bryant's legacy was tarnished.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:39.240
He was charged with sexually assaulting

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.430
a 19-year-old hotel employee.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:44.070
Bryant, his wife Vanessa beside him said

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.810
the sexual encounter was consensual.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.990
Prosecutors eventually
dropped all criminal charges

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:51.320
when the women said she
didn't want to testify.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.940
Bryant later settled a civil
suit connected to the case.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.291
Back on the court, he
continued breaking records.

00:01:57.291 --> 00:02:01.170
In 2006, he scored 81
points in a single game,

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:03.040
the second highest in NBA history.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.030
- I couldn't even dream
of this when I was a kid.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.670
There's just no way possible.

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:09.400
- [Reporter] In 2008, he
was named the league's MVP

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.120
but he couldn't take his team all the way

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.330
to victory that year.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.372
- That was a turning point.

00:02:13.372 --> 00:02:16.149
It was when I sat there in
the hotel room afterwards,

00:02:16.149 --> 00:02:18.654
I started thinking about that

00:02:18.654 --> 00:02:20.360
'cause it's on me.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.520
If I didn't feel like my
teammates were aggressive enough,

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:24.100
that falls on me.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.620
And I had to understand
what their journey was,

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:27.860
how are they feeling as people,

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.150
what are they going through?

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.518
- [Reporter] The next year,
the Lakers were back on top.

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:33.930
He won his fourth championship

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:36.863
and in 2010, his fifth and final.

00:02:37.831 --> 00:02:40.520
- Championships are a byproduct of things,

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:43.292
drills and exercises that I
did when I was six years old.

00:02:43.292 --> 00:02:44.590
(chuckling)

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:48.800
- [Reporter] In 2016 after 20
years in the NBA, he retired.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.260
- [Jason] The thing
that I will never forget

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:52.260
is his last game in the NBA.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.570
He got 60 points off 50 shots

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.570
which is a spectacular amount of shots

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.374
to take in a basketball game.

00:02:58.374 --> 00:03:01.813
- [Reporter] What an exit for number 24!

00:03:01.813 --> 00:03:04.970
- [Jason] It's kind of in
this very small moment,

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:06.297
in his last moment of the court,

00:03:06.297 --> 00:03:08.224
the NBA kind of in miniature,

00:03:08.224 --> 00:03:10.740
all the greatnesses and brilliances

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.217
and excesses of what it
meant to be Kobe Bryant.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:15.553
- [Reporter] After leaving the court,

00:03:15.553 --> 00:03:17.960
Bryant turned his attention
to new business endeavors.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.070
He launched a venture capital firm,

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.570
published a series of
young adult fantasy novels

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:24.100
and even won an academy award

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.170
for an animated short film
called "Dear Basketball,"

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:29.282
an ode to his love for the game.

00:03:29.282 --> 00:03:31.570
- [Kobe] My heart can take the pounding.

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:34.030
My mind can handle the grind.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:36.180
But my body knows it's
time to say goodbye.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:41.070
- [Reporter] When the LA Lakers
retired his jersey numbers

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:44.160
in 2017, Bryant reminded his daughters

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.350
of the secrets of his success.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:49.060
- You guys know that if you do the work,

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.330
you work hard enough, dreams come true.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.320
You know that, we all know that

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.390
but hopefully want you get from tonight

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:58.423
is the understanding that those times

00:03:58.423 --> 00:04:00.634
when you get up early and you work hard,

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:02.430
those times where you stay up late

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:03.893
and you work hard, those times

00:04:03.893 --> 00:04:05.420
when you don't feel like working,

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:06.980
you're too tired, you
don't wanna push yourself

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.373
but you do it anyway,

00:04:08.373 --> 00:04:11.209
that is actually the dream.

00:04:11.209 --> 00:04:13.130
That's the dream,

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:15.280
it's not the destination,
it's the journey.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:18.150
- [Reporter] Kobe was recently spotted out

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:21.600
at NBA games with his
13-year-old daughter Gianna

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.150
who died alongside him in the crash.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:27.450
She was a rising star
basketball player herself.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.960
- It was 20 great years.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.360
It was very fortunate to play that long.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:34.180
And but now I watch it
through my daughter.

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:35.430
My daughter plays every day.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:37.178
- [Reporter] He called her mambacita,

00:04:37.178 --> 00:04:40.340
a nod to the nickname
he had given himself.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:43.813
- Mamba out.
(crowd cheering)

00:04:44.875 --> 00:04:47.875
(melancholic music)

